NAME
    queue - the runner's slots, and a slot for a heavy job

SYNOPSIS
    queue
    queue ask CLASS [--gb N] [--as WHO]

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module. The desktop's slots per class
    (two cpu, one gpu, from ~/.config/EmuSen/testing/runners.json) are
    lock files under ~/.cache/emusen/testing/queue/, held with flock(2).
    trial takes a cpu slot for each step and waits for one otherwise.

    queue lists every slot, tab-separated: class, slot, held or free, and
    who holds it and since when, as the holder wrote it.

    queue ask waits until a slot of CLASS is free and prints a command
    prefix: flock on that slot, then systemd-run --user --scope with
    CPUWeight=20, MemoryMax=N G (default 10) and MemorySwapMax=2G. The
    command run after it holds the slot for as long as it runs; if another
    job took the slot in between, flock waits. Each ask is a row of the
    store's queue table.

    When the household's lease service arrives, the one function that
    takes a slot calls it instead of the lock files. See EmuSen_Testing.md
    §3.8.

EXAMPLES
    queue
    $(dianash -c 'queue ask cpu --gb 8 --as studio-p1') cargo build --release
